WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.220
- But I also heard that COVID

00:00:02.220 --> 00:00:03.900
has hit close to home with you,

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:06.180
so you have loved ones
working in the hospitals

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:07.160
right now, right?

00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:09.710
- Yeah, well it hasn't
hit, so far, thank God.

00:00:09.710 --> 00:00:14.657
Like touch wood, I'm like,
my sister is a midwife

00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:17.700
with the National Health Service here,

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:20.974
and my partner's sister and stepmother

00:00:20.974 --> 00:00:24.360
are both NHS nurses as well.

00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:27.789
So between the three of us we've got three

00:00:27.789 --> 00:00:31.680
members of family that
are, you know, well,

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:35.260
front line in the community or a hospital.

00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:37.620
So I don't know how often you guys do it,

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:39.590
but we go outside and, you know,

00:00:39.590 --> 00:00:42.730
bang for, clap for carers,
bang our pots and pans,

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:45.680
and clap for our National
Health Service staff

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:49.170
and our carers every Thursday evening,

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:52.150
and so we're out there giving it loads,

00:00:52.150 --> 00:00:54.670
and, you know, we just
worry about them, because,

00:00:54.670 --> 00:00:55.920
but I'm so proud.

00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:58.638
I'm so ridiculously proud,
Kelly, of my sister.

00:00:58.638 --> 00:01:01.430
And she was an elderly
carer in the community

00:01:01.430 --> 00:01:02.470
before she was a midwife.

00:01:02.470 --> 00:01:03.710
She's just one of those people

00:01:03.710 --> 00:01:05.080
that's just, like, she's just--

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:06.040
- [Kelly] A nurturer.

00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:07.000
- Yeah, she's a nurturer.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:09.010
And she's just so good, and she has,

00:01:09.010 --> 00:01:10.510
she just has that capacity.

00:01:10.510 --> 00:01:13.940
Enormous mental, as well
as physical capacity,

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:15.680
and I know it's the same with you guys,

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:17.340
your side of the pond as us.

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:19.550
It's like, to our medical staff,

00:01:19.550 --> 00:01:21.180
we are just so indebted.

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:23.880
- Yeah, 'cause you didn't, it's weird,

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:25.530
but we didn't even think
about it before, you know,

00:01:25.530 --> 00:01:27.580
we always, I take my kids,
you know, to the doctor,

00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:28.413
I do all this stuff, you know,

00:01:28.413 --> 00:01:29.860
you always go to the doctor,
you don't think about it,

00:01:29.860 --> 00:01:31.810
but God, this is really opened your eyes

00:01:31.810 --> 00:01:34.890
to how much of a servants
heart they all have.

00:01:34.890 --> 00:01:35.820
- Yeah.

00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:38.610
- 'Cause a lot of these
nurses have kids and families

00:01:38.610 --> 00:01:40.400
and, you know, they
don't wanna bring it home

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:41.400
and infect their families.

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:43.960
So, it's just a different
level of sacrifice

00:01:43.960 --> 00:01:45.971
that none of us will ever know.

00:01:45.971 --> 00:01:46.804
- [Natalie] Yeah, it's so true.

00:01:46.804 --> 00:01:50.434
David, my partner, his sister
has got two kids under five.

00:01:50.434 --> 00:01:53.080
And she's, you know,
front line as a nurse.

00:01:53.080 --> 00:01:55.570
And I'm just like, you know,
it's like, what do I do?

00:01:55.570 --> 00:01:56.770
I make stories for a living.

00:01:56.770 --> 00:01:58.870
It's like, it really does help you,

00:01:58.870 --> 00:02:01.640
I mean I know people need
escapism, and it's cool.

00:02:01.640 --> 00:02:04.377
- Beautiful distraction,
like that's a, don't--

